        "senderName": "NWS Charleston WV",
        "headline": "Flood Warning issued September 21 at 9:08PM EDT until September 22 at 9:45AM EDT by NWS Charleston WV",
        "description": "* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues.\n\n* WHERE...North Central Athens County in southeastern Ohio...\n\n* WHEN...Until 945 AM EDT Tuesday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding of Sunday Creek and it's tributaries is\noccurring. Numerous roads remain closed due to flooding.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 905 PM EDT, The Ohio Department of Transportation reported\nseveral roads remain closed due to flooding from Sunday Creek.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nGlouster, Jacksonville and Trimble.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
        "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.",
